  "description": "Production-grade Firebase Cloud Messaging (push notifications) for .NET: automatic batching over FCM's 500-token limit, dead-token reporting, topic broadcast, retry with backoff, explicit fail-open behaviour, and an optional built-in device-token store (generic-key, provider-neutral, self-migrating) that owns the FirebaseUserDevices table, prunes dead tokens, keeps an in-app inbox, and audits every send.",
  "id": "AQZ.Firebase.Toolkit",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-09-10T11:33:31.757Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "LyFnGgBBkM5bBN4Lj49/B/Zt8u8Mp8kbnC96jzvPL5InQ074LifQYTR1vYY9t+X37uRnkGMV8RZQ9NKo5djHLA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 83602,
  "published": "2026-09-10T11:30:24.69Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "3.6.0: IUserPushService gains a BroadcastAsync overload that excludes a caller-supplied set of user ids (BroadcastAsync(message, excludeUserIds, ct)), so a consuming app can honour a per-user notification preference on broadcast without the toolkit knowing what a preference is. Backed by a new repository query (GetActiveTokensPagedExcludingUsersAsync). No schema change, no migration; non-breaking. 3.5.0: the send audit gains a first-class Category (event-type) column on FirebaseNotificationDispatches, populated from the message data key (FirebaseStoreOptions.CategoryDataKey, default \"category\") and filterable via NotificationDispatchQuery.Category, so admin history can be filtered by event type without parsing JSON. Adds a column + index: generate one store migration after upgrading. Non-breaking. 3.4.0: complete send auditing across all audiences (Users, Broadcast, Tokens, Topic, Condition) into FirebaseNotificationDispatches. 3.3.0: data/options types unsealed for inheritance.",
